# ── Voltx Database Backup Schedule ───────────────────────────────────
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Do not install it directly — the bracketed
# tokens below are substituted with absolute paths for this machine by:
#
#   deploy/scripts/install-backup-schedule.sh            # install
#   deploy/scripts/install-backup-schedule.sh --print    # preview only
#   crontab -l                                           # verify
#
# The previous version of this file shipped `/path/to/deploy` placeholders and
# invited `crontab deploy/crontab`. Installing it produced a schedule that
# failed on every single run — backups appeared scheduled and were not. The
# installer exists so that can no longer happen silently.
#
# Both jobs take the same exclusive lock *inside the scripts themselves*
# (deploy/scripts/with-lock.sh, atomic mkdir — no flock dependency), so a
# slow backup can never overlap the next one, the weekly verification can
# never race a backup, and a manual run is protected too. LOCK_DIR selects
# where the lock lives.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
MAILTO=""

# ── Daily database backup — 03:00 UTC ────────────────────────────────
# Retention is enforced by backup.sh (BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS, default 14).
0 3 * * * BACKUP_DIR=__BACKUP_DIR__ BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=__RETENTION_DAYS__ COMPOSE_FILE=__DEPLOY_DIR__/docker-compose.yml LOCK_DIR=__LOCK_DIR__ __DEPLOY_DIR__/scripts/backup.sh --docker >> __LOG_DIR__/backup.log 2>&1

# ── Weekly backup-integrity verification — Sunday 05:00 UTC ──────────
# Restores the most recent archive into a disposable database and proves it
# is actually usable: decompresses, restores, and the expected tables,
# foreign keys, indexes and sequences all survive. A backup that has never
# been restored is a hypothesis, not a capability.
0 5 * * 0 LOCK_DIR=__LOCK_DIR__ __DEPLOY_DIR__/scripts/verify-latest-backup.sh __BACKUP_DIR__ >> __LOG_DIR__/backup-verify.log 2>&1
